# Working agreement

- Work on a feature branch named `feature/ui-*`, `feature/backend-*`, or
  `fix/*`. Never commit directly to `main`.
- For UI-only tasks, change only `app/**`, `src/components/**`, and
  `src/theme/**` unless the user explicitly approves a broader scope.
- Do not modify `supabase/**`, RLS, authentication, membership, RevenueCat, or
  `src/lib/**` during UI work.
- Never expose a secret, service-role key, password, or unrestricted API key.
- Do not add direct Supabase calls to screens or components. Use the existing
  data-access functions in `src/lib/**`.
- Do not introduce demo bypasses into production paths.
- Do not upgrade dependencies or install packages without approval.
- Preserve strict TypeScript behavior; do not silence errors with `any`,
  `@ts-ignore`, or disabled compiler rules.
- Run `npm run check` before handing work back. Report any failure honestly.
- Keep pull requests small and include screenshots for visual changes.
